# The seam wolf (as02b): the wolf-lang commit that carries the driver's
# assembler seam, `wolf build --assembler PATH` over `WOLF_AS` over the
# legacy C driver, a selected assembler's failure final (wolf-lang#957,
# as02a, merged at 9f2cff44; R-as02-1 A). No release carries it yet, so
# tests/kernel-as builds this commit from source by tools/fetch-wolf's
# SOURCE shape (PAX_WOLF_PIN names this file), and nothing else does:
# kernel/wolf.pin stays the 0.2.35 release every kernel and image is
# built with (R-as02-5 A). The freestanding runtime is not rebuilt:
# crates/wolf_rt_none is the same tree at v0.2.35 and at this commit
# (`git diff v0.2.35 9f2cff44 -- crates/wolf_rt_none` is empty), so the
# suite stages kernel/wolf.pin's archive's libwolf_rt_none.a beside the
# built binary, the bytes every kernel already links. When a release
# carries #957, kernel/wolf.pin moves to it and this file goes.
WOLF_LANG_COMMIT=9f2cff44c945697903e52ea7e5fdf05539b207ae
# load_wolf_pin needs lupin's lines in every pin; kernel/wolf.pin's.
LUPIN_VERSION=0.1.56
LUPIN_SHA256=ad703550ac4787e8e4bb26989d591a731410274d7332f2b4e8b9a64c878822cc
